<body>
<h1 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.1px 0.0px; font: 24.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #138756; -webkit-text-stroke: #138756"><span class="s1"><b>How Much Should a Deck Cost to Build in 2026? Real Prices Per Square Foot</b></span></h1>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><i>Meta Title: Deck Building Cost 2026: Real Prices Per Square Foot (Wood vs Composite)</i> <i>Meta Description: Planning a deck? See actual cost breakdowns for materials, labor, permits, and installation. Compare wood vs composite decking with regional price adjustments.</i></span></p>
<p class="p3"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">You want a deck. You've measured the space. You've imagined summer evenings out there. Now you need to know: <b>what's this actually going to cost?</b></span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">National averages say "$30-$60 per square foot"—but that range is so wide it's basically useless. Let's get specific.</span></p>
<h2 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.9px 0.0px; font: 18.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0f6745; -webkit-text-stroke: #0f6745"><span class="s1"><b>The Quick Numbers</b></span></h2>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">For a <b>300 sqft deck</b> (10' x 30', typical size):</span></p>
<table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="t1">
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td1">
        <p class="p5"><span class="s1"><b>Material Type</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td2">
        <p class="p5"><span class="s1"><b>DIY Cost</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td3">
        <p class="p5"><span class="s1"><b>Pro Install</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td4">
        <p class="p5"><span class="s1"><b>Total (Pro)</b></span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td5">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1"><b>Pressure-treated wood</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td6">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$4,500-6,000</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td7">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$3,600-4,500</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td8">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$8,100-10,500</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td5">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1"><b>Cedar/Redwood</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td6">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$7,500-9,000</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td7">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$3,900-4,800</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td8">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$11,400-13,800</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td5">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1"><b>Composite (mid-grade)</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td6">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$9,000-12,000</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td7">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$4,200-5,400</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td8">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$13,200-17,400</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td5">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1"><b>Composite (premium)</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td6">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$12,000-15,000</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td7">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$4,500-6,000</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td8">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$16,500-21,000</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td5">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1"><b>PVC/vinyl</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td6">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$13,500-16,500</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td7">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$4,800-6,300</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td8">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$18,300-22,800</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><i>Includes: Framing, joists, decking, railings, stairs, hardware, labor. Does NOT include: Permits, site prep, electrical, or water features.</i></span></p>
<p class="p3"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h2 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.9px 0.0px; font: 18.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0f6745; -webkit-text-stroke: #0f6745"><span class="s1"><b>Cost Breakdown: What You're Actually Paying For</b></span></h2>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>1. Materials (50-60% of total cost)</b></span></h3>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Framing &amp; Structure ($8-12/sqft)</b></span></h4>
<ul class="ul1">
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"><b></b></span><span class="s1"><b>Pressure-treated lumber for joists:</b> $1.50-2.50/linear foot (2x8)</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"><b></b></span><span class="s1"><b>Posts (4x4 or 6x6):</b> $12-35 each</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"><b></b></span><span class="s1"><b>Beams (2x10 or larger):</b> $15-40 per beam</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"><b></b></span><span class="s1"><b>Concrete footings:</b> $8-15 per footing (you'll need 8-12 for a 300 sqft deck)</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"><b></b></span><span class="s1"><b>Joist hangers, bolts, brackets:</b> $200-400 for typical deck</span></li>
</ul>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>What's fair:</b> Framing should account for roughly 30-35% of your material cost.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Red flag:</b> If a quote says "structure included" with no itemization, ask for specifics. Under-engineered framing is a safety hazard.</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Decking Surface ($4-25/sqft)</b></span></h4>
<table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="t1">
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td9">
        <p class="p5"><span class="s1"><b>Material</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td10">
        <p class="p5"><span class="s1"><b>Cost/sqft</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td11">
        <p class="p5"><span class="s1"><b>Lifespan</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td12">
        <p class="p5"><span class="s1"><b>Maintenance</b></span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td13">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1"><b>Pressure-treated pine</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td14">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$4-7</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td15">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">15-20 yrs</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td16">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">High (annual sealing)</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td13">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1"><b>Cedar</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td14">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$8-12</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td15">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">20-25 yrs</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td16">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">Medium (stain every 2-3 yrs)</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td13">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1"><b>Redwood</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td14">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$10-15</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td15">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">25-30 yrs</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td16">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">Medium</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td13">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1"><b>Composite (Trex, TimberTech)</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td14">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$10-18</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td15">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">25-30 yrs</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td16">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">Low (clean annually)</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td13">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1"><b>PVC (Azek, Fiberon)</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td14">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$15-25</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td15">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">30+ yrs</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td16">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">Very low</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td13">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1"><b>Ipe/tropical hardwood</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td14">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$18-30</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td15">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">30-50 yrs</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td16">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">Low-medium</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Pro tip:</b> Budget composite decking often uses cheaper materials that fade faster. Mid-grade composite ($12-15/sqft) is the sweet spot for value.</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Railings &amp; Stairs ($1,500-5,000 total)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Railing costs (per linear foot):</b> - Pressure-treated wood balusters: $20-35/ft - Composite with aluminum balusters: $50-80/ft - Cable railing (stainless steel): $60-100/ft - Glass panel railing: $150-300/ft</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Stairs:</b> - 3-4 step staircase (pressure-treated): $400-700 - 5-6 step staircase (composite): $800-1,400</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Code requirement:</b> Most jurisdictions require railings if the deck is more than 30" above grade. Budget for it.</span></p>
<p class="p3"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>2. Labor (30-40% of total cost)</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Deck building labor rates (2026):</span></p>
<table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="t1">
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td17">
        <p class="p5"><span class="s1"><b>Region</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td18">
