      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td21">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1"><b>Mountain West</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td22">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$40</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td23">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$60</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td24">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$80</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td21">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1"><b>Northeast, Pacific NW</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td22">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$50</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td23">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$75</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td24">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$100</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td21">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1"><b>CA, NYC metro</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td22">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$65</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td23">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$90</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td24">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$130</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Typical crew:</b> 2-3 workers for 3-5 days (depending on size and complexity).</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>What's fair:</b> For a 300 sqft deck, expect 60-100 labor hours total ($3,000-7,500 depending on region).</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Red flag:</b> If labor is quoted at less than 25% of total cost, the contractor may be: - Planning to cut corners - Using inexperienced crew - Underestimating complexity (change orders coming later)</span></p>
<p class="p3"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>3. Permits &amp; Fees (5-10% of total cost)</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Don't skip permits. Seriously.</span></p>
<table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="t1">
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td25">
        <p class="p5"><span class="s1"><b>Permit Type</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td26">
        <p class="p5"><span class="s1"><b>Typical Cost</b></span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td27">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1"><b>Building permit</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td28">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$150-500</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td27">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1"><b>Engineering/structural review</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td28">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$300-800 (if required)</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td27">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1"><b>HOA approval</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td28">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$0-200 (some HOAs charge admin fees)</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Why it matters:</b> - Un-permitted decks must often be torn down when discovered - Affects home insurance coverage - Becomes a liability when selling - Can void warranties on materials</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>What's fair:</b> Contractor should pull permits and include cost in quote. If they suggest skipping permits "to save money," walk away.</span></p>
<p class="p3"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>4. Site Prep &amp; Extras</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">These are often NOT included in base quotes:</span></p>
<table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="t1">
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td29">
        <p class="p5"><span class="s1"><b>Item</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td30">
        <p class="p5"><span class="s1"><b>Cost</b></span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
