<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>Labor</b></span></h3>
<ul class="ul1">
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">2-person crew, 4 days (64 hours @ $55/hr avg): <b>$3,520</b></span></li>
</ul>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>Permits &amp; Fees</b></span></h3>
<ul class="ul1">
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Building permit: <b>$225</b></span></li>
</ul>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>Total: $13,313</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Per square foot:</b> $44.38</span></p>
<p class="p3"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h2 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.9px 0.0px; font: 18.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0f6745; -webkit-text-stroke: #0f6745"><span class="s1"><b>How to Tell If Your Deck Quote Is Fair</b></span></h2>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>1. Check the material markup</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Contractors typically mark up materials by 10-20%. You can verify retail prices: - Lowe's/Home Depot for common materials - Local lumber yards for framing - Manufacturer websites for composite decking MSRP</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Red flag:</b> Material costs 40%+ above retail (unless it's specialized/custom product).</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>2. Verify labor hours match scope</b></span></h3>
<table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="t1">
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td41">
        <p class="p5"><span class="s1"><b>Deck Size</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td42">
        <p class="p5"><span class="s1"><b>Typical Labor Hours</b></span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td43">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">100-200 sqft</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td44">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">30-50 hours</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td43">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">200-300 sqft</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td44">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">50-80 hours</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td43">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">300-400 sqft</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td44">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">70-100 hours</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td43">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">400+ sqft</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td44">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">90-130+ hours</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Add hours for:</b> - Complex shapes (angles, curves, multiple levels): +20-40% - Elevated decks (8'+ above grade): +30-50% - Stairs, built-ins, pergolas: +15-30% each</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>3. Compare apples to apples</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">When comparing three quotes:</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">✅ <b>Do:</b> - Confirm same decking material (or equivalent grade) - Verify same railing style - Check if permits are included - Ask if stairs are included - Confirm warranty coverage</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">❌ <b>Don't:</b> - Compare PT wood quote to composite quote - Assume "same" materials without brand/model names - Ignore differences in railing quality</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>4. Watch for lowball traps</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">If one quote is 30%+ cheaper than others:</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Possible explanations:</b> - Different materials (PT wood vs composite, or lower-grade composite) - Thinner joists/wider spacing (not to code) - Skipping permits - Inexperienced crew - Planning to upsell with change orders</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>What to ask:</b> - "What joist spacing are you using?" (16" on-center is standard, 24" is weaker) - "What fastener type?" (hidden clips cost more but look better) - "Are permits included?" - "What's your warranty on workmanship?"</span></p>
<p class="p3"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h2 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.9px 0.0px; font: 18.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0f6745; -webkit-text-stroke: #0f6745"><span class="s1"><b>Regional Price Adjustments</b></span></h2>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Multiply base costs by these factors:</span></p>
<table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="t1">
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td45">
        <p class="p5"><span class="s1"><b>Region</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td46">
        <p class="p5"><span class="s1"><b>Multiplier</b></span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td47">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1"><b>Rural Midwest/South</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td48">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">0.85x</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td47">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1"><b>Mid-size cities</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td48">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">1.0x (baseline)</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td47">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1"><b>Denver, Seattle, Portland</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td48">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">1.15x</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td47">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1"><b>Boston, DC, Philadelphia</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td48">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">1.25x</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td47">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1"><b>San Francisco Bay Area</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td48">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">1.45x</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td47">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1"><b>New York City metro</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td48">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">1.55x</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Example:</b> A $12,000 deck in Columbus, OH would cost ~$17,400 in Boston, or ~$18,600 in SF.</span></p>
<p class="p3"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h2 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.9px 0.0px; font: 18.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0f6745; -webkit-text-stroke: #0f6745"><span class="s1"><b>What's NOT Included in Most Quotes</b></span></h2>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Unless explicitly stated, assume these are extra:</span></p>
<ul class="ul1">
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Gas/water line relocation</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Irrigation system adjustments</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Landscaping around deck</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Outdoor kitchen/BBQ hookups</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Hot tub reinforcement (requires extra structural support)</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Snow load engineering (in heavy snow regions)</span></li>
</ul>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Pro tip:</b> Ask for a written scope of work that lists what IS and ISN'T included.</span></p>
<p class="p3"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h2 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.9px 0.0px; font: 18.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0f6745; -webkit-text-stroke: #0f6745"><span class="s1"><b>When to DIY vs Hire a Pro</b></span></h2>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>DIY makes sense if:</b></span></h3>
<ul class="ul1">
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">You have carpentry experience</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">You own/can borrow necessary tools (circular saw, drill, level, post-hole digger)</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">The deck is ground-level (&lt; 30" high, no railings required)</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">You have time (20-40 hours for a 200 sqft deck)</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">You're comfortable pulling permits and arranging inspections</span></li>
</ul>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Savings:</b> 30-40% on labor (but factor in tool costs and your time).</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>Hire a pro if:</b></span></h3>
<ul class="ul1">
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Deck is elevated (safety risk if framing fails)</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Local code is complex</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">You need engineering (steep slope, heavy snow loads)</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">You want warranty protection</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Your time is worth more than $40-60/hr</span></li>
</ul>
<p class="p3"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h2 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.9px 0.0px; font: 18.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0f6745; -webkit-text-stroke: #0f6745"><span class="s1"><b>Questions to Ask Before You Sign</b></span></h2>
<ol class="ol1">
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"><b></b></span><span class="s1"><b>"Can I see the itemized material list with brands/models?"</b></span></li>
  <li class="li2"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">If they won't provide it, walk away.</span></li>
  <li class="li2"><span class="s2"><b></b></span><span class="s1"><b>"What's your payment schedule?"</b></span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Standard: 10-20% deposit, 40% at demo/framing, 40% at completion.</span></li>
  <li class="li2"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Red flag: 50%+ upfront.</span></li>
  <li class="li2"><span class="s2"><b></b></span><span class="s1"><b>"Are permits included?"</b></span></li>
  <li class="li2"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">If no, get permit cost estimate in writing.</span></li>
  <li class="li2"><span class="s2"><b></b></span><span class="s1"><b>"What warranty do you offer on workmanship?"</b></span></li>
  <li class="li2"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Industry standard: 1-2 years on labor.</span></li>
  <li class="li2"><span class="s2"><b></b></span><span class="s1"><b>"What's your joist spacing and beam size?"</b></span></li>
  <li class="li2"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Should match local code (typically 16" on-center for joists).</span></li>
  <li class="li2"><span class="s2"><b></b></span><span class="s1"><b>"Do you carry general liability and workers' comp insurance?"</b></span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Ask for proof. If they're uninsured and someone gets hurt, you're liable.</span></li>
</ol>
<p class="p3"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h2 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.9px 0.0px; font: 18.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0f6745; -webkit-text-stroke: #0f6745"><span class="s1"><b>How Ungouge.ai Can Help</b></span></h2>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Instead of guessing whether your deck quote is fair, <b>upload it to Ungouge.ai</b>.</span></p>
