<p class="p10"><span class="s3">Get your deck quote analyzed →</span></p>
<p class="p3"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h2 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.9px 0.0px; font: 18.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0f6745; -webkit-text-stroke: #0f6745"><span class="s1"><b>Bottom Line</b></span></h2>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">For a typical <b>300 sqft composite deck</b> with railings and stairs: - <b>Budget range:</b> $12,000-17,000 (including labor, materials, permits) - <b>Cost per sqft:</b> $40-57</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">If your quote is significantly higher, it should include: - Premium materials (high-end composite, cable/glass railings) - Complex design (multi-level, curves, built-ins) - Difficult site conditions (steep slope, limited access) - Regional cost adjustment (high-cost metro area)</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>If it's higher without those factors, you're likely being overcharged.</b></span></p>
